# Hermes provider

The Hermes provider manages durable Hermes dashboard configuration through its authenticated management API.

## Example usage

{{tffile "examples/example_1.tf"}}

The provider accepts `HERMES_DASHBOARD_URL`, `HERMES_DASHBOARD_USERNAME`, and `HERMES_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD` environment variables. Prefer environment variables or an external secret manager for machine credentials.

## Resources

- [`hermes_model_assignment`](resources/model_assignment.md) assigns a main or auxiliary Hermes model.
- [`hermes_custom_provider`](resources/custom_provider.md) manages a named OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
- [`hermes_profile`](resources/profile.md) manages a named Hermes profile.
- [`hermes_mcp_server`](resources/mcp_server.md) manages an HTTP/SSE MCP registration.
- [`hermes_cron_job`](resources/cron_job.md) manages a durable Hermes cron job.
- [`hermes_messaging_platform`](resources/messaging_platform.md) manages a fixed messaging platform without storing credentials in state.
- [`hermes_skill`](resources/skill.md) manages activation state for an existing skill.
- [`hermes_skill_installation`](resources/skill_installation.md) manages a scanned skill-hub installation.
- [`hermes_toolset`](resources/toolset.md) manages a built-in toolset toggle.
- [`hermes_plugin`](resources/plugin.md) manages an explicitly reviewed agent-plugin installation.

## Data sources

- [`hermes_model_options`](data-sources/model_options.md) reads available provider/model options.
- [`hermes_status`](data-sources/status.md) reads non-secret Hermes and gateway status.

Dashboard-only plugin discovery remains outside the resource surface because
it is filesystem-backed and not generic CRUD. See
[`docs/v0.1.0-scope.md`](https://github.com/stevenhansel/terraform-provider-hermes/blob/main/docs/v0.1.0-scope.md) for the implementation contract.

